{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-114699" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the integral $\\int (1-2{x}^{2}){e}^{4x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012723/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb29f9257d8d370df29c95874be5cdb0bc94457616e43c9e2dd7525e61d0d866"} {"question" "q-114699" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We need to use integration by parts.\n\nIn this case, we define\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=1-2{x}^{2}\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-4x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{4x}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int {e}^{4x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (1-2{x}^{2}){e}^{4x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(1-2{x}^{2})(\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{4})-\\int (\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{4})(-4x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{(1-2{x}^{2}){e}^{4x}}{4}+\\int x{e}^{4x}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe use integration by parts once again to evaluate $\\int x{e}^{4x}\\,\\text{d}x.$ We take\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{4x}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int {e}^{4x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the formula for integration by parts gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x{e}^{4x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x(\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{4})-\\int (\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{4})(1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{x{e}^{4x}}{4}-\\frac{1}{4}\\int {e}^{4x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{x{e}^{4x}}{4}-\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{16}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{16}(4x-1)+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an integral constant.\n\nSo we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (1-2{x}^{2}){e}^{4x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{(1-2{x}^{2}){e}^{4x}}{4}+(\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{16}(4x-1)+C) \\\\  & =\\frac{(1-2{x}^{2}){e}^{4x}}{4}+\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{16}(4x-1)+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{16}(-8{x}^{2}+4x+3)+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012723/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb29f9257d8d370df29c95874be5cdb0bc94457616e43c9e2dd7525e61d0d866"} {"question" "q-114699" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012723/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "73e2e5d6ad4967d7751ef0e1dbef63ab5f4bc0743b1a19fe41d4aaf281d1bc56"} {"question" "q-114699" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012723/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb29f9257d8d370df29c95874be5cdb0bc94457616e43c9e2dd7525e61d0d866"} {"question" "q-114699" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{16}(-4{x}^{2}+2x+1)+C"] ["math" "\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{16}(-8{x}^{2}+4x+3)+C"] ["math" "\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{4}(4{x}^{2}-2x+1)+C"] ["math" "\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{8}(-4{x}^{2}+2x+3)+C"] ["math" "\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{8}(2{x}^{2}+x+4)+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012723/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb29f9257d8d370df29c95874be5cdb0bc94457616e43c9e2dd7525e61d0d866"} {"question" "q-114699" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{16}(-8{x}^{2}+4x+3)+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012723/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb29f9257d8d370df29c95874be5cdb0bc94457616e43c9e2dd7525e61d0d866"} {"question" "q-352110" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{1}({x}^{2}+5){e}^{2x+2}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012723/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb29f9257d8d370df29c95874be5cdb0bc94457616e43c9e2dd7525e61d0d866"} {"question" "q-352110" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We need to use integration by parts. We'll work out the indefinite integral first, and then proceed to work out the definite integral.\n\nIn this case, we define\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={x}^{2}+5\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2x, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{2x+2}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int {e}^{2x+2}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{{e}^{2x+2}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ({x}^{2}+5){e}^{2x+2}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =({x}^{2}+5)(\\frac{{e}^{2x+2}}{2})-\\int (\\frac{{e}^{2x+2}}{2})(2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{({x}^{2}+5){e}^{2x+2}}{2}-\\int x\\,{e}^{2x+2}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe use integration by parts once again to evaluate $\\int x\\,{e}^{2x+2}\\,\\text{d}x.$ We take\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{2x+2}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int {e}^{2x+2}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{{e}^{2x+2}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the formula for integration by parts gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x\\,{e}^{2x+2}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(x)(\\frac{{e}^{2x+2}}{2})-\\int (\\frac{{e}^{2x+2}}{2})(1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{x\\,{e}^{2x+2}}{2}-\\frac{1}{2}\\int {e}^{2x+2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{x\\,{e}^{2x+2}}{2}-\\frac{{e}^{2x+2}}{4}+D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is a constant. \n\nSo, we get that the indefinite integral is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ({x}^{2}+5){e}^{2x+2}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{({x}^{2}+5){e}^{2x+2}}{2}-\\int x\\,{e}^{2x+2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{({x}^{2}+5){e}^{2x+2}}{2}-(\\frac{x\\,{e}^{2x+2}}{2}-\\frac{{e}^{2x+2}}{4}+D) \\\\  & =\\frac{({x}^{2}+5){e}^{2x+2}}{2}-\\frac{x\\,{e}^{2x+2}}{2}+\\frac{{e}^{2x+2}}{4}-D \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2x+2}}{4}(2{x}^{2}-2x+11)+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=-D.$ \n\nFinally then, we can work out the definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}({x}^{2}+5){e}^{2x+2}\\,\\text{d}x & ={[\\frac{{e}^{2x+2}}{4}(2{x}^{2}-2x+11)]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =(\\frac{{e}^{2(1)+2}}{4}(2(1)^{2}-2(1)+11))-(\\frac{{e}^{2(0)+2}}{4}(2(0)^{2}-2(0)+11)) \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{4}}{4}(2-2+11)-\\frac{{e}^{2}}{4}(0-0+11) \\\\  & =\\frac{11{e}^{4}}{4}-\\frac{11{e}^{2}}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{11{e}^{4}-11{e}^{2}}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012723/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb29f9257d8d370df29c95874be5cdb0bc94457616e43c9e2dd7525e61d0d866"} {"question" "q-352110" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012723/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "73e2e5d6ad4967d7751ef0e1dbef63ab5f4bc0743b1a19fe41d4aaf281d1bc56"} {"question" "q-352110" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012723/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb29f9257d8d370df29c95874be5cdb0bc94457616e43c9e2dd7525e61d0d866"} {"question" "q-352110" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{11e^4-11e^2}{4}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012723/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb29f9257d8d370df29c95874be5cdb0bc94457616e43c9e2dd7525e61d0d866"} {"question" "q-12703" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\int 5{x}^{2}{e}^{3x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012723/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb29f9257d8d370df29c95874be5cdb0bc94457616e43c9e2dd7525e61d0d866"} {"question" "q-12703" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We need to use integration by parts.\n\nIn this case, we define\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=5{x}^{2}\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=10x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{3x}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int {e}^{3x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{{e}^{3x}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 5{x}^{2}{e}^{3x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(5{x}^{2})(\\frac{{e}^{3x}}{3})-\\int (\\frac{{e}^{3x}}{3})(10x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{5{x}^{2}{e}^{3x}}{3}-\\frac{10}{3}\\int x{e}^{3x}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe use integration by parts once again to evaluate $\\int x{e}^{3x}\\,\\text{d}x.$ We take\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{3x}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int {e}^{3x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{{e}^{3x}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the formula for integration by parts gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x{e}^{3x}\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x(\\frac{{e}^{3x}}{3})-\\int (\\frac{{e}^{3x}}{3})(1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{x{e}^{3x}}{3}-\\frac{1}{3}\\int {e}^{3x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{x{e}^{3x}}{3}-\\frac{{e}^{3x}}{9}+D \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{3x}}{9}(3x-1)+D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is an integral constant.\n\nSo we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 5{x}^{2}{e}^{3x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{5{x}^{2}{e}^{3x}}{3}-\\frac{10}{3}(\\frac{{e}^{3x}}{9}(3x-1)+D) \\\\  & =\\frac{5{x}^{2}{e}^{3x}}{3}-\\frac{10{e}^{3x}}{27}(3x-1)-\\frac{10D}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{5{e}^{3x}}{27}(9{x}^{2}-6x+2)+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=-\\frac{10D}{3}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012723/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb29f9257d8d370df29c95874be5cdb0bc94457616e43c9e2dd7525e61d0d866"} {"question" "q-12703" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012723/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "73e2e5d6ad4967d7751ef0e1dbef63ab5f4bc0743b1a19fe41d4aaf281d1bc56"} {"question" "q-12703" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012723/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb29f9257d8d370df29c95874be5cdb0bc94457616e43c9e2dd7525e61d0d866"} {"question" "q-12703" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{5{e}^{3x}}{27}(3{x}^{2}+3x-2)+C"] ["math" "\\frac{5{e}^{3x}}{27}(3{x}^{2}-2x+1)+C"] ["math" "\\frac{5{e}^{3x}}{27}(9{x}^{2}-6x+2)+C"] ["math" "\\frac{5{e}^{3x}}{9}(3{x}^{2}+6x-2)+C"] ["math" "\\frac{5{e}^{3x}}{9}(6{x}^{2}-3x+1)+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012723/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb29f9257d8d370df29c95874be5cdb0bc94457616e43c9e2dd7525e61d0d866"} {"question" "q-12703" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{5{e}^{3x}}{27}(9{x}^{2}-6x+2)+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012723/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb29f9257d8d370df29c95874be5cdb0bc94457616e43c9e2dd7525e61d0d866"} {"question" "q-351977" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{1}{t}^{2}{e}^{4t}\\,\\text{d}t=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012723/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb29f9257d8d370df29c95874be5cdb0bc94457616e43c9e2dd7525e61d0d866"} {"question" "q-351977" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We need to use integration by parts. We'll work out the indefinite integral first, and then proceed to work out the definite integral.\n\nIn this case, we define\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={t}^{2}\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t}=2t, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}={e}^{4t}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t=\\int {e}^{4t}\\,\\text{d}t=\\frac{1}{4}{e}^{4t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {t}^{2}{e}^{4t}\\,\\text{d}t & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =({t}^{2})(\\frac{1}{4}{e}^{4t})-\\int (\\frac{1}{4}{e}^{4t})(2t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{t}^{2}{e}^{4t}-\\frac{1}{2}\\int t{e}^{4t}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe use integration by parts once again to evaluate $\\int t{e}^{4t}\\,\\text{d}t.$ We take\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=t\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t}=1, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}={e}^{4t}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t=\\int {e}^{4t}\\,\\text{d}t=\\frac{1}{4}{e}^{4t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the formula for integration by parts gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int t{e}^{4t}\\,\\text{d}t & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =(t)(\\frac{1}{4}{e}^{4t})-\\int (\\frac{1}{4}{e}^{4t})(1)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}t{e}^{4t}-\\frac{1}{4}\\int {e}^{4t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}t{e}^{4t}-\\frac{1}{16}{e}^{4t}+D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is a constant. \n\nSo, we get that the indefinite integral is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {t}^{2}{e}^{4t}\\,\\text{d}t & =\\frac{1}{4}{t}^{2}{e}^{4t}-\\frac{1}{2}\\int t{e}^{4t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{t}^{2}{e}^{4t}-\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{1}{4}t{e}^{4t}-\\frac{1}{16}{e}^{4t}+D) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{t}^{2}{e}^{4t}-\\frac{1}{8}t{e}^{4t}+\\frac{1}{32}{e}^{4t}+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=-\\frac{D}{2}.$\n\nFinally, we can work out the definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{t}^{2}{e}^{4t}\\,\\text{d}t & =(\\frac{1}{4}{t}^{2}{e}^{4t}-\\frac{1}{8}t{e}^{4t}+\\frac{1}{32}{e}^{4t})\\,{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{4}({1}^{2}){e}^{4}-\\frac{1}{8}(1){e}^{4}+\\frac{1}{32}{e}^{4})-(\\frac{1}{4}({0}^{2}){e}^{0}-\\frac{1}{8}(0){e}^{0}+\\frac{1}{32}{e}^{0}) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{32}{e}^{4}-\\frac{1}{32} \\\\  & =\\frac{5{e}^{4}-1}{32}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012723/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb29f9257d8d370df29c95874be5cdb0bc94457616e43c9e2dd7525e61d0d866"} {"question" "q-351977" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012723/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "73e2e5d6ad4967d7751ef0e1dbef63ab5f4bc0743b1a19fe41d4aaf281d1bc56"} {"question" "q-351977" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012723/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb29f9257d8d370df29c95874be5cdb0bc94457616e43c9e2dd7525e61d0d866"} {"question" "q-351977" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{5e^4-1}{32}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012723/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb29f9257d8d370df29c95874be5cdb0bc94457616e43c9e2dd7525e61d0d866"} {"question" "q-114695" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\int ({x}^{2}-4){e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012723/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb29f9257d8d370df29c95874be5cdb0bc94457616e43c9e2dd7525e61d0d866"} {"question" "q-114695" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We need to use integration by parts.\n\nIn this case, we define\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={x}^{2}-4\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{x}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int {e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x={e}^{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ({x}^{2}-4){e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =({x}^{2}-4)({e}^{x})-\\int ({e}^{x})(2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =({x}^{2}-4){e}^{x}-2\\int x{e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe use integration by parts once again to evaluate $\\int x{e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x.$ We take\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{x}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int {e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x={e}^{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the formula for integration by parts gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x{e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x({e}^{x})-\\int ({e}^{x})(1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x{e}^{x}-\\int {e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x{e}^{x}-{e}^{x}+D \\\\  & ={e}^{x}(x-1)+D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is an integral constant.\n\nSo we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ({x}^{2}-4){e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =({x}^{2}-4){e}^{x}-2({e}^{x}(x-1)+D) \\\\  & =({x}^{2}-4){e}^{x}-2(x-1){e}^{x}-2D \\\\  & ={e}^{x}({x}^{2}-2x-2)+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=-2D.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012723/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb29f9257d8d370df29c95874be5cdb0bc94457616e43c9e2dd7525e61d0d866"} {"question" "q-114695" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012723/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "73e2e5d6ad4967d7751ef0e1dbef63ab5f4bc0743b1a19fe41d4aaf281d1bc56"} {"question" "q-114695" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012723/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb29f9257d8d370df29c95874be5cdb0bc94457616e43c9e2dd7525e61d0d866"} {"question" "q-114695" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{e}^{x}(2{x}^{2}-x+2)+C"] ["math" "{e}^{x}(3{x}^{2}-x-1)+C"] ["math" "{e}^{x}(4{x}^{2}-4x-1)+C"] ["math" "{e}^{x}({x}^{2}-2x-2)+C"] ["math" "{e}^{x}({x}^{2}-x+1)+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012723/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb29f9257d8d370df29c95874be5cdb0bc94457616e43c9e2dd7525e61d0d866"} {"question" "q-114695" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{e}^{x}({x}^{2}-2x-2)+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012723/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb29f9257d8d370df29c95874be5cdb0bc94457616e43c9e2dd7525e61d0d866"} {"question" "q-352030" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012723/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb29f9257d8d370df29c95874be5cdb0bc94457616e43c9e2dd7525e61d0d866"} {"question" "q-352030" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We need to use integration by parts. We'll work out the indefinite integral first, and then proceed to work out the definite integral.\n\nIn this case, we define\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=2{x}^{2}\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=4x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x=-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(2{x}^{2})(-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{2})-\\int (-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{2})(4x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)+2\\int x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAgain, we use integration by parts to evaluate $\\int x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x.$ We take\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x & \\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1\\,, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x) & \\,⟹\\,v=\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\text{d}x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the formula for integration by parts gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x(\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{2})-\\int (\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{2})\\cdot 1\\,dx \\\\  & =\\frac{x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{2}+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{4}+D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is an integral constant. \n\nSo, we get that the indefinite integral is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)+2\\int x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)+2(\\frac{x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{2}+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{4}+D) \\\\  & =-{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)+x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{2}+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=2D.$\n\nFinally, then, we can work out the definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={[-{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)+x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{2}]}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =(-{(\\frac{\\pi }{2})}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi )+(\\frac{\\pi }{2})\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi )}{2}) \\\\  & \\,-(-(0)^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)+(0)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)}{2}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{4}-\\frac{1}{2})-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{4}-1 \\\\  & =\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{4}-1\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012723/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb29f9257d8d370df29c95874be5cdb0bc94457616e43c9e2dd7525e61d0d866"} {"question" "q-352030" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012723/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "73e2e5d6ad4967d7751ef0e1dbef63ab5f4bc0743b1a19fe41d4aaf281d1bc56"} {"question" "q-352030" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012723/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb29f9257d8d370df29c95874be5cdb0bc94457616e43c9e2dd7525e61d0d866"} {"question" "q-352030" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\pi^2}{4}-1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012723/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb29f9257d8d370df29c95874be5cdb0bc94457616e43c9e2dd7525e61d0d866"} {"question" "q-352118" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }3{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012723/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb29f9257d8d370df29c95874be5cdb0bc94457616e43c9e2dd7525e61d0d866"} {"question" "q-352118" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We need to use integration by parts. We'll work out the indefinite integral first, and then proceed to work out the definite integral.\n\nIn this case, we define\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=3{x}^{2}\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=6x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 3{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(3{x}^{2})(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x))-\\int (\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x))(6x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)-6\\int x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAgain, we use integration by parts to evaluate $\\int x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x.$ We take\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x & \\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1\\,, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x) & \\,⟹\\,v=\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\text{d}x=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the formula for integration by parts gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x))-\\int (-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x))\\cdot 1\\,dx \\\\  & =-x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,dx \\\\  & =-x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is an integral constant. \n\nSo, we get that the indefinite integral is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 3{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =3{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)-6\\int x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)-6(-x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+D) \\\\  & =3{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+6x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=-6D.$\n\nFinally, we can work out the definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }3{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={[3{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+6x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)]}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =(3(\\pi )^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )+6(\\pi )\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi )-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi ))-(3(0)^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)+6(0)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =0+6\\pi (-1)-0-0 \\\\  & =-6\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012723/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb29f9257d8d370df29c95874be5cdb0bc94457616e43c9e2dd7525e61d0d866"} {"question" "q-352118" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012723/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "73e2e5d6ad4967d7751ef0e1dbef63ab5f4bc0743b1a19fe41d4aaf281d1bc56"} {"question" "q-352118" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012723/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb29f9257d8d370df29c95874be5cdb0bc94457616e43c9e2dd7525e61d0d866"} {"question" "q-352118" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-6\\pi"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012723/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb29f9257d8d370df29c95874be5cdb0bc94457616e43c9e2dd7525e61d0d866"} {"question" "q-50233" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int {x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-1)\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012723/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb29f9257d8d370df29c95874be5cdb0bc94457616e43c9e2dd7525e61d0d866"} {"question" "q-50233" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We need to use integration by parts. \n\nIn this case, we define\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={x}^{2}\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-1)\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-1)\\,\\text{d}x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-1)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =({x}^{2})(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-1))-\\int (\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-1)(2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-1)-2\\int x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-1)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAgain, we use integration by parts to evaluate $\\int x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-1)\\text{d}x.$ We take\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-1)\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-1)\\,\\text{d}x=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the formula for integration by parts gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-1)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(x)(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-1))-\\int (-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-1))(1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-1)+\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-1)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-1)+D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is an integral constant.\n\nSo we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-1)\\,\\text{d}x & ={x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-1)-2(-x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-1)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-1)+D) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-1)+2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-1)-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-1)-2D \\\\  & =({x}^{2}-2)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-1)+2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-1)+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=-2D.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012723/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb29f9257d8d370df29c95874be5cdb0bc94457616e43c9e2dd7525e61d0d866"} {"question" "q-50233" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012723/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "73e2e5d6ad4967d7751ef0e1dbef63ab5f4bc0743b1a19fe41d4aaf281d1bc56"} {"question" "q-50233" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012723/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb29f9257d8d370df29c95874be5cdb0bc94457616e43c9e2dd7525e61d0d866"} {"question" "q-50233" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(2{x}^{2}+1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-1)+2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-1)+C"] ["math" "({x}^{2}+1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-1)-x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-1)+C"] ["math" "({x}^{2}-2)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-1)+2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-1)+C"] ["math" "2({x}^{2}-1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-1)+{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-1)+C"] ["math" "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-1)+{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-1)+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012723/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb29f9257d8d370df29c95874be5cdb0bc94457616e43c9e2dd7525e61d0d866"} {"question" "q-50233" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "({x}^{2}-2)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-1)+2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-1)+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012723/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb29f9257d8d370df29c95874be5cdb0bc94457616e43c9e2dd7525e61d0d866"} {"question" "q-50222" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int {x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012723/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb29f9257d8d370df29c95874be5cdb0bc94457616e43c9e2dd7525e61d0d866"} {"question" "q-50222" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We need to use integration by parts. \n\nIn this case, we define\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={x}^{2}\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x=-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =({x}^{2})(-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3})-\\int (-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3})(2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3}+\\frac{2}{3}\\int x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012723/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb29f9257d8d370df29c95874be5cdb0bc94457616e43c9e2dd7525e61d0d866"} {"question" "q-50222" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012723/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "73e2e5d6ad4967d7751ef0e1dbef63ab5f4bc0743b1a19fe41d4aaf281d1bc56"} {"question" "q-50222" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012723/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb29f9257d8d370df29c95874be5cdb0bc94457616e43c9e2dd7525e61d0d866"} {"question" "q-50222" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3}+\\frac{2}{3}\\int x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x"] ["math" "-\\frac{{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3}+\\frac{2}{3}\\int x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x"] ["math" "-\\frac{{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{2}+\\frac{3}{2}\\int x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x"] ["math" "\\frac{{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3}+\\frac{1}{3}\\int x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x"] ["math" "\\frac{{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3}-\\frac{2}{3}\\int x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012723/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb29f9257d8d370df29c95874be5cdb0bc94457616e43c9e2dd7525e61d0d866"} {"question" "q-50222" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3}+\\frac{2}{3}\\int x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012723/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb29f9257d8d370df29c95874be5cdb0bc94457616e43c9e2dd7525e61d0d866"} {"question" "q-352007" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(5{x}^{2}+6)\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012723/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb29f9257d8d370df29c95874be5cdb0bc94457616e43c9e2dd7525e61d0d866"} {"question" "q-352007" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We need to use integration by parts. We'll work out the indefinite integral first, and then proceed to work out the definite integral.\n\nIn this case, we define\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=5{x}^{2}+6\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=10x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (5{x}^{2}+6)\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(5{x}^{2}+6)(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)-\\int (-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)(10x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-(5{x}^{2}+6)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+10\\int x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAgain, we use integration by parts to evaluate $\\int x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.$ We take\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x & \\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1\\,, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x & \\,⟹\\,v=\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the formula for integration by parts gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,dx \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is an integral constant. \n\nSo, we get that the indefinite integral is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (5{x}^{2}+6)\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =-(5{x}^{2}+6)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+10\\int x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-(5{x}^{2}+6)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+10(x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+D) \\\\  & =-(5{x}^{2}+6)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+10x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+10\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=10D.$\n\nFinally, we can work out the definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(5{x}^{2}+6)\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & ={[-(5{x}^{2}+6)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+10x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+10\\operatorname{cos}⁡x]}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =(-(5{(\\frac{\\pi }{2})}^{2}+6)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{2}+10(\\frac{\\pi }{2})\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{2}+10\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{2})-(-6\\operatorname{cos}⁡0+10(0)\\operatorname{sin}⁡0+10\\operatorname{cos}⁡0) \\\\  & =(0+5\\pi +0)-(-6+10) \\\\  & =5\\pi -4 \\\\  & =5\\pi -4\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012723/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb29f9257d8d370df29c95874be5cdb0bc94457616e43c9e2dd7525e61d0d866"} {"question" "q-352007" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012723/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "73e2e5d6ad4967d7751ef0e1dbef63ab5f4bc0743b1a19fe41d4aaf281d1bc56"} {"question" "q-352007" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012723/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb29f9257d8d370df29c95874be5cdb0bc94457616e43c9e2dd7525e61d0d866"} {"question" "q-352007" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "5\\pi-4"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012723/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb29f9257d8d370df29c95874be5cdb0bc94457616e43c9e2dd7525e61d0d866"} {"question" "q-114942" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate ${\\int }_{1}^{e}9{x}^{2}({log}_{2}⁡x)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012723/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb29f9257d8d370df29c95874be5cdb0bc94457616e43c9e2dd7525e61d0d866"} {"question" "q-114942" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We need to use integration by parts. We'll work out the indefinite integral first, and then proceed to work out the definite integral.\n\nIn this case, we define\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=({log}_{2}⁡x)^{2}\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2{log}_{2}⁡x}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡2} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=9{x}^{2}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int 9{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x=3{x}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 9{x}^{2}({log}_{2}⁡x)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={({log}_{2}⁡x)}^{2}(3{x}^{3})-\\int (3{x}^{3})(\\frac{2{log}_{2}⁡x}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3{x}^{3}{({log}_{2}⁡x)}^{2}-\\frac{6}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\int {x}^{2}{log}_{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe use integration by parts once again to evaluate  $\\int {x}^{2}{log}_{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.$ We take\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={log}_{2}⁡x\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡2} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}={x}^{2}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the formula for integration by parts gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {x}^{2}{log}_{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =({log}_{2}⁡x)(\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3})-\\int (\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3})(\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{3}{log}_{2}⁡x}{3}-\\frac{1}{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{3}{log}_{2}⁡x}{3}-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{9\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}+D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is an integral constant.\n\nSo we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 9{x}^{2}({log}_{2}⁡x)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x & =3{x}^{3}{({log}_{2}⁡x)}^{2}-\\frac{6}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(\\frac{{x}^{3}{log}_{2}⁡x}{3}-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{9\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}+D) \\\\  & =3{x}^{3}{({log}_{2}⁡x)}^{2}-\\frac{2{x}^{3}{log}_{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}+\\frac{2{x}^{3}}{3{ln}^{2}⁡2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{3{x}^{3}{ln}^{2}⁡x}{{ln}^{2}⁡2}-\\frac{2{x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{{ln}^{2}⁡2}+\\frac{2{x}^{3}}{3{ln}^{2}⁡2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{3}}{{ln}^{2}⁡2}(3{ln}^{2}⁡x-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+\\frac{2}{3})+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=-\\frac{6D}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}.$\n\nNote that in the above calculation we used the change of base formula ${log}_{2}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}.$\n\nFinally then, we can work out the definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{e}9{x}^{2}({log}_{2}⁡x)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x & ={[\\frac{{x}^{3}}{{ln}^{2}⁡2}(3{ln}^{2}⁡x-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+\\frac{2}{3})]}_{1}^{e} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{3}}{{ln}^{2}⁡2}(3{ln}^{2}⁡e-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡e+\\frac{2}{3})-\\frac{{1}^{3}}{{ln}^{2}⁡2}(3{ln}^{2}⁡1-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡1+\\frac{2}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{3}}{{ln}^{2}⁡2}(3-2+\\frac{2}{3})-\\frac{1}{{ln}^{2}⁡2}(0-0+\\frac{2}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{5{e}^{3}}{3{ln}^{2}⁡2}-\\frac{2}{3{ln}^{2}⁡2} \\\\  & =\\frac{5{e}^{3}-2}{3{ln}^{2}⁡2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012723/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb29f9257d8d370df29c95874be5cdb0bc94457616e43c9e2dd7525e61d0d866"} {"question" "q-114942" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012723/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "73e2e5d6ad4967d7751ef0e1dbef63ab5f4bc0743b1a19fe41d4aaf281d1bc56"} {"question" "q-114942" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012723/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb29f9257d8d370df29c95874be5cdb0bc94457616e43c9e2dd7525e61d0d866"} {"question" "q-114942" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2{e}^{2}+3"] ["math" "4{e}^{3}-1"] ["math" "\\frac{2{e}^{2}-3}{4{ln}^{2}⁡2}"] ["math" "\\frac{5{e}^{3}-2}{3{ln}^{2}⁡2}"] ["math" "\\frac{{e}^{3}-1}{{ln}^{2}⁡2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012723/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb29f9257d8d370df29c95874be5cdb0bc94457616e43c9e2dd7525e61d0d866"} {"question" "q-114942" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{5{e}^{3}-2}{3{ln}^{2}⁡2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012723/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb29f9257d8d370df29c95874be5cdb0bc94457616e43c9e2dd7525e61d0d866"} {"question" "q-114883" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate ${\\int }_{1}^{e}{ln}^{2}⁡({x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012723/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb29f9257d8d370df29c95874be5cdb0bc94457616e43c9e2dd7525e61d0d866"} {"question" "q-114883" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We need to use integration by parts. We'll work out the indefinite integral first, and then proceed to work out the definite integral.\n\nIn this case, we define\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={ln}^{2}⁡({x}^{3})\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{6\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})}{x} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=1\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\,\\text{d}x=x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {ln}^{2}⁡({x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =({ln}^{2}⁡({x}^{3}))(x)-\\int (x)(\\frac{6\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})}{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x{ln}^{2}⁡({x}^{3})-6\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe use integration by parts once again to evaluate $\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})\\text{d}x.$ We take\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{3}{x} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=1\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\,\\text{d}x=x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the formula for integration by parts gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3}))(x)-\\int (x)(\\frac{3}{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})-3\\int \\text{d}x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})-3x+D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is a constant. \n\nSo, we get that the indefinite integral is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {ln}^{2}⁡({x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x & =x{ln}^{2}⁡({x}^{3})-6(x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})-3x+D) \\\\  & =x{ln}^{2}⁡({x}^{3})-6x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})+18x+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=-6D.$ \n\nFinally then, we can work out the definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{e}{ln}^{2}⁡({x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x & ={[x{ln}^{2}⁡({x}^{3})-6x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})+18x]}_{1}^{e} \\\\  & =[e{ln}^{2}⁡({e}^{3})-6e\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{3})+18e]-[(1){ln}^{2}⁡({1}^{3})-6(1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡({1}^{3})+18(1)] \\\\  & =9e-18e+18e-18 \\\\  & =9e-18.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012723/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb29f9257d8d370df29c95874be5cdb0bc94457616e43c9e2dd7525e61d0d866"} {"question" "q-114883" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012723/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "73e2e5d6ad4967d7751ef0e1dbef63ab5f4bc0743b1a19fe41d4aaf281d1bc56"} {"question" "q-114883" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012723/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb29f9257d8d370df29c95874be5cdb0bc94457616e43c9e2dd7525e61d0d866"} {"question" "q-114883" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "3e+9"] ["math" "3e-9"] ["math" "9e+12"] ["math" "9e-18"] ["math" "e-18"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012723/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb29f9257d8d370df29c95874be5cdb0bc94457616e43c9e2dd7525e61d0d866"} {"question" "q-114883" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "9e-18"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012723/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb29f9257d8d370df29c95874be5cdb0bc94457616e43c9e2dd7525e61d0d866"} {"question" "q-114944" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate ${\\int }_{1}^{e}{({log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2}))}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012723/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb29f9257d8d370df29c95874be5cdb0bc94457616e43c9e2dd7525e61d0d866"} {"question" "q-114944" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We need to use integration by parts. We'll work out the indefinite integral first, and then proceed to work out the definite integral.\n\nIn this case, we define\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={({log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2}))}^{2}\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{4{log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2})}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡3} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=1\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\,\\text{d}x=x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {({log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2}))}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x{({log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2}))}^{2}-\\int (x)(\\frac{4{log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2})}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x{({log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2}))}^{2}-\\frac{4}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\int {log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe use integration by parts once again to evaluate  $\\int {log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x.$ We take\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2})\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡3} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=1\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\,\\text{d}x=x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the formula for integration by parts gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =({log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2}))(x)-\\int (x)(\\frac{2}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x{log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2})-\\frac{2}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x{log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2})-\\frac{2x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is an integral constant.\n\nSo we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {({log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2}))}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x & =x{({log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2}))}^{2}-\\frac{4}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}(x{log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2})-\\frac{2x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+D) \\\\  & =x{({log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2}))}^{2}-\\frac{4x{log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2})}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+\\frac{8x}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{x{ln}^{2}⁡({x}^{2})}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}-\\frac{4x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}+\\frac{8x}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{x}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}({ln}^{2}⁡({x}^{2})-4\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})+8)+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=-\\frac{4D}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}.$\n\nNote that in the above calculation we used the change of base formula ${log}_{3}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}.$\n\nFinally then, we can work out the definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{e}{({log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2}))}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x & ={[\\frac{x}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}({ln}^{2}⁡({x}^{2})-4\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})+8)]}_{1}^{e} \\\\  & =\\frac{e}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}({ln}^{2}⁡({e}^{2})-4\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{2})+8)-\\frac{1}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}({ln}^{2}⁡({1}^{2})-4\\operatorname{ln}⁡({1}^{2})+8) \\\\  & =\\frac{e}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}(4-8+8)-\\frac{1}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}(0-0+8) \\\\  & =\\frac{4e-8}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012723/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb29f9257d8d370df29c95874be5cdb0bc94457616e43c9e2dd7525e61d0d866"} {"question" "q-114944" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012723/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "73e2e5d6ad4967d7751ef0e1dbef63ab5f4bc0743b1a19fe41d4aaf281d1bc56"} {"question" "q-114944" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012723/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb29f9257d8d370df29c95874be5cdb0bc94457616e43c9e2dd7525e61d0d866"} {"question" "q-114944" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2{e}^{2}+6"] ["math" "3{e}^{2}-2"] ["math" "\\frac{4e+3}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}"] ["math" "\\frac{4e-8}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}"] ["math" "\\frac{e-6}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012723/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb29f9257d8d370df29c95874be5cdb0bc94457616e43c9e2dd7525e61d0d866"} {"question" "q-114944" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{4e-8}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012723/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb29f9257d8d370df29c95874be5cdb0bc94457616e43c9e2dd7525e61d0d866"} {"question" "q-352049" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{1/3}^{e/3}243{x}^{2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x))^{2}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012723/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb29f9257d8d370df29c95874be5cdb0bc94457616e43c9e2dd7525e61d0d866"} {"question" "q-352049" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We'll work out the indefinite integral first, and then proceed to work out the definite integral.\n\nIn this case, we define\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x))^{2} & \\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)}{x}\\,, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=243{x}^{2} & \\,⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int 243{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x=81{x}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 243{x}^{2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x))^{2}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x))}^{2}(81{x}^{3})-\\int (81{x}^{3})(\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)}{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =81{x}^{3}{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x))}^{2}-162\\int {x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe use integration by parts once again to evaluate $\\int {x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x.$ We take\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x) & \\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}\\,, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}={x}^{2} & \\,⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the formula for integration by parts gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)(\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3})-\\int (\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3})(\\frac{1}{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)}{3}-\\frac{1}{3}\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)}{3}-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{9}+D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is an integral constant. \n\nSo, we get that the indefinite integral is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 243{x}^{2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x))^{2}\\,\\text{d}x & =81{x}^{3}{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x))}^{2}-162\\int {x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =81{x}^{3}{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x))}^{2}-162(\\frac{{x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)}{3}-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{9}+D) \\\\  & =81{x}^{3}{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x))}^{2}-54{x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)+18{x}^{3}-162D \\\\  & ={x}^{3}(81{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x))}^{2}-54\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)+18)+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=-162D.$\n\nFinally, we can work out the definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1/3}^{e/3}243{x}^{2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x))^{2}\\text{d}x & ={[{x}^{3}(81{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x))}^{2}-54\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)+18)]}_{1/3}^{e/3} \\\\  & =[{(\\frac{e}{3})}^{3}(81{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3\\cdot \\frac{e}{3}))}^{2}-54\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3\\cdot \\frac{e}{3})+18)] \\\\  & \\,-[{(\\frac{1}{3})}^{3}(81{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}))}^{2}-54\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3\\cdot \\frac{1}{3})+18)] \\\\  & =[\\frac{{e}^{3}}{27}(81{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡e)}^{2}-54\\operatorname{ln}⁡e+18)]-[\\frac{1}{27}(81{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡1)}^{2}-54\\operatorname{ln}⁡1+18)] \\\\  & =[\\frac{{e}^{3}}{27}(81-54+18)]-\\frac{1}{27}\\cdot 18 \\\\  & =\\frac{5{e}^{3}-2}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012723/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb29f9257d8d370df29c95874be5cdb0bc94457616e43c9e2dd7525e61d0d866"} {"question" "q-352049" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012723/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "73e2e5d6ad4967d7751ef0e1dbef63ab5f4bc0743b1a19fe41d4aaf281d1bc56"} {"question" "q-352049" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012723/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb29f9257d8d370df29c95874be5cdb0bc94457616e43c9e2dd7525e61d0d866"} {"question" "q-352049" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{5e^3-2}{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012723/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb29f9257d8d370df29c95874be5cdb0bc94457616e43c9e2dd7525e61d0d866"} {"question" "q-12708" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the integral $\\int ({log}_{3}⁡x)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012723/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb29f9257d8d370df29c95874be5cdb0bc94457616e43c9e2dd7525e61d0d866"} {"question" "q-12708" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We need to use integration by parts.\n\nIn this case, we define\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=({log}_{3}⁡x)^{2}\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2{log}_{3}⁡x}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡3} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=1\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\,\\text{d}x=x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ({log}_{3}⁡x)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={({log}_{3}⁡x)}^{2}(x)-\\int (x)(\\frac{2{log}_{3}⁡x}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x{({log}_{3}⁡x)}^{2}-\\frac{2}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\int {log}_{3}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe use integration by parts once again to evaluate  $\\int {log}_{3}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x.$ We take\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={log}_{3}⁡(x)\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡3} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=1\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\,\\text{d}x=x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the formula for integration by parts gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {log}_{3}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =({log}_{3}⁡(x))(x)-\\int (x)(\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x{log}_{3}⁡(x)-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x{log}_{3}⁡(x)-\\frac{x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is an integral constant.\n\nSo we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ({log}_{3}⁡x)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x & =x{({log}_{3}⁡x)}^{2}-\\frac{2}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}(x{log}_{3}⁡(x)-\\frac{x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+D) \\\\  & =x{({log}_{3}⁡x)}^{2}-\\frac{2x{log}_{3}⁡(x)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+\\frac{2x}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}-\\frac{2D}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3} \\\\  & =x({({log}_{3}⁡x)}^{2}-\\frac{2{log}_{3}⁡(x)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+\\frac{2}{{ln}^{2}⁡3})+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=-\\frac{2D}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012723/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb29f9257d8d370df29c95874be5cdb0bc94457616e43c9e2dd7525e61d0d866"} {"question" "q-12708" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012723/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "73e2e5d6ad4967d7751ef0e1dbef63ab5f4bc0743b1a19fe41d4aaf281d1bc56"} {"question" "q-12708" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012723/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb29f9257d8d370df29c95874be5cdb0bc94457616e43c9e2dd7525e61d0d866"} {"question" "q-12708" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2x(3{({log}_{3}⁡x)}^{2}+\\frac{{log}_{3}⁡(x)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+\\frac{2}{{ln}^{2}⁡3})+C"] ["math" "2x({({log}_{3}⁡x)}^{2}-\\frac{{log}_{3}⁡(x)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}-\\frac{1}{{ln}^{2}⁡3})+C"] ["math" "x({({log}_{3}⁡x)}^{2}+\\frac{2{log}_{3}⁡(x)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}-\\frac{2}{{ln}^{2}⁡3})+C"] ["math" "x({({log}_{3}⁡x)}^{2}-\\frac{2{log}_{3}⁡(x)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+\\frac{2}{{ln}^{2}⁡3})+C"] ["math" "x({({log}_{3}⁡x)}^{2}-\\frac{3{log}_{3}⁡(x)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+\\frac{3}{{ln}^{2}⁡3})+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012723/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb29f9257d8d370df29c95874be5cdb0bc94457616e43c9e2dd7525e61d0d866"} {"question" "q-12708" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x({({log}_{3}⁡x)}^{2}-\\frac{2{log}_{3}⁡(x)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+\\frac{2}{{ln}^{2}⁡3})+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012723/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb29f9257d8d370df29c95874be5cdb0bc94457616e43c9e2dd7525e61d0d866"} {"question" "e-7053" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the integral $\\displaystyle \\int_0^1 (t^2+1)e^{2t+1} \\, \\textrm{d} t.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012723/example-7053.json" "file_sha256" "fe38e0123e0de33f6eb8e4b1b99e4f444e4212906e0b71f21ee73167a8c9a9c8"} {"question" "e-7053" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We need to use integration by parts. We'll work out the indefinite integral first, and then proceed to work out the definite integral.\n\nIn this case, we define\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={t}^{2}+1\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t}=2t, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}={e}^{2t+1}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t=\\int {e}^{2t+1}\\,\\text{d}t=\\frac{{e}^{2t+1}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ({t}^{2}+1){e}^{2t+1}\\,\\text{d}t & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =({t}^{2}+1)(\\frac{{e}^{2t+1}}{2})-\\int (\\frac{{e}^{2t+1}}{2})(2t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{({t}^{2}+1){e}^{2t+1}}{2}-\\int t\\,{e}^{2t+1}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe use integration by parts once again to evaluate $\\displaystyle\\int t\\,e^{2t+1}\\,\\textrm{d}t.$ We take\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=t\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t}=1 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}={e}^{2t+1}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t=\\int {e}^{2t+1}\\,\\text{d}t=\\frac{{e}^{2t+1}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the formula for integration by parts gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int t\\,{e}^{2t+1}\\,\\text{d}t & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =(t)(\\frac{{e}^{2t+1}}{2})-\\int (\\frac{{e}^{2t+1}}{2})(1)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{t\\,{e}^{2t+1}}{2}-\\frac{1}{2}\\int {e}^{2t+1}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{t\\,{e}^{2t+1}}{2}-\\frac{{e}^{2t+1}}{4}+D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is a constant. \n\nSo, we get that the indefinite integral is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ({t}^{2}+1){e}^{2t+1}\\,\\text{d}t & =\\frac{({t}^{2}+1){e}^{2t+1}}{2}-\\int t\\,{e}^{2t+1}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{({t}^{2}+1){e}^{2t+1}}{2}-(\\frac{t\\,{e}^{2t+1}}{2}-\\frac{{e}^{2t+1}}{4}+D) \\\\  & =\\frac{({t}^{2}+1){e}^{2t+1}}{2}-\\frac{t\\,{e}^{2t+1}}{2}+\\frac{{e}^{2t+1}}{4}-D \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2t+1}}{4}(2{t}^{2}-2t+3)+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C = -{D}.$ \n\nFinally then, we can work out the definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}({t}^{2}+1){e}^{2t+1}\\,\\text{d}t & ={[\\frac{{e}^{2t+1}}{4}(2{t}^{2}-2t+3)]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =(\\frac{{e}^{2(1)+1}}{4}(2(1)^{2}-2(1)+3))-(\\frac{{e}^{2(0)+1}}{4}(2(0)^{2}-2(0)+3)) \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{3}}{4}(2-2+3)-\\frac{e}{4}(0-0+3) \\\\  & =\\frac{3{e}^{3}}{4}-\\frac{3e}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{3{e}^{3}-3e}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012723/example-7053.json" "file_sha256" "fe38e0123e0de33f6eb8e4b1b99e4f444e4212906e0b71f21ee73167a8c9a9c8"} {"question" "e-495" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the integral $\\displaystyle \\int x^2\\cos(3x) \\textrm{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012723/example-495.json" "file_sha256" "c2560714d737412ad6c32ca7148380ba79fd8de1a0a5d6db76e4616f4f726585"} {"question" "e-495" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "In this case, we define\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={x}^{2} & \\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2x\\,, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x) & \\,⟹\\,v=\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{3}\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =({x}^{2})(\\frac{1}{3}\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x))-\\int (\\frac{1}{3}\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x))2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)-\\frac{2}{3}\\int x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAgain, we use integration by parts to evaluate $\\displaystyle \\int x\\sin(3x) \\textrm{d}x.$ We take\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x & \\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1\\,, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x) & \\,⟹\\,v=\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\text{d}x=-\\,\\frac{1}{3}\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the formula for integration by parts gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x(-\\,\\frac{1}{3}\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x))-\\int (-\\,\\frac{1}{3}\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x))\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\,\\frac{1}{3}\\,x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)+\\frac{1}{3}\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\,\\frac{1}{3}\\,x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)+\\frac{1}{3}(\\frac{1}{3}\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x))+{C}_{1} \\\\  & =-\\,\\frac{1}{3}\\,x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)+\\frac{1}{9}\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+{C}_{1}\\,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C_1$ is a constant of integration.\nSo we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)-\\frac{2}{3}\\int x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)-\\frac{2}{3}(-\\,\\frac{1}{3}\\,x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)+\\frac{1}{9}\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+{C}_{1}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+\\frac{2}{9}x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)-\\frac{2}{27}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)-\\frac{2{C}_{1}}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{27}((9{x}^{2}-2)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+6x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x))+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C = -\\dfrac{2C_1}{3}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012723/example-495.json" "file_sha256" "c2560714d737412ad6c32ca7148380ba79fd8de1a0a5d6db76e4616f4f726585"} {"question" "e-496" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the integral $\\displaystyle \\int_1^e 32x^3(\\ln x)^2 \\textrm{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012723/example-496.json" "file_sha256" "9e543c7bb30ddfd20cf829e256641be203761b075cd6ed45507374baebd7ae55"} {"question" "e-496" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We'll work out the indefinite integral first, and then proceed to work out the definite integral.\n\nIn this case, we define\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)^{2} & \\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{x}\\,, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=32{x}^{3} & \\,⟹\\,v=\\int 32{x}^{3}\\text{d}x=8{x}^{4}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 32{x}^{3}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)^{2}\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}^{2}(8{x}^{4})-\\int (8{x}^{4})(\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{x})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =8{x}^{4}{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}^{2}-16\\int {x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe use integration by parts once again to evaluate $\\displaystyle\\int {x^3\\ln(x)} \\textrm{d}x.$ We take\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x) & \\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}\\,, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}={x}^{3} & \\,⟹\\,v=\\int {x}^{3}\\text{d}x=\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the formula for integration by parts gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)(\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4})-\\int (\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4})(\\frac{1}{x})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)}{4}-\\frac{1}{4}\\int {x}^{3}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)}{4}-\\frac{{x}^{4}}{16}+{C}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C_1$ is an integral constant. So, we get that the indefinite integral is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 32{x}^{3}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)^{2}\\text{d}x & =8{x}^{4}{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}^{2}-16\\int {x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =8{x}^{4}{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}^{2}-16(\\frac{{x}^{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)}{4}-\\frac{{x}^{4}}{16}+{C}_{1}) \\\\  & =8{x}^{4}{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}^{2}-4{x}^{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)+{x}^{4}-16{C}_{1} \\\\  & ={x}^{4}(8{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}^{2}-4\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)+1)+C\\,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C = -4C_1.$ Finally then, we can work out the definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{e}32{x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\text{d}x & ={{x}^{4}(8{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}^{2}-4\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)+1)|}_{1}^{e} \\\\  & =[(e)^{4}(8{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(e))}^{2}-4\\operatorname{ln}⁡(e)+1)]-[(1)^{4}(8{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1))}^{2}-4\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1)+1)] \\\\  & =[{e}^{4}(8-4+1)]-1 \\\\  & =5{e}^{4}-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012723/example-496.json" "file_sha256" "9e543c7bb30ddfd20cf829e256641be203761b075cd6ed45507374baebd7ae55"}] "usage" {"e-7053" [] "e-495" [] "e-496" []} "basis" 1159 "retractions" [[17592186068560 :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int x^2e^{2x}\\, \\textrm{d}x$."] [17592186068560 :question/worked-solution "We need to use integration by parts.\n\nIn this case, we define\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}u = x^{2} & ⟹\\frac{du}{dx} = 2x \\\\ \\frac{dv}{dx} = e^{2x} & ⟹v = \\int\\frac{dv}{dx}dx = \\inte^{2x}dx = \\frac{e^{2x}}{2}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\intx^{2}e^{2x}dx &= \\intu\\frac{dv}{dx}dx \\\\\n&= uv - \\intv\\frac{du}{dx}dx \\\\\n&= (x^{2})(\\frac{e^{2x}}{2}) - \\int(\\frac{e^{2x}}{2})(2x)dx \\\\\n&= \\frac{x^{2}e^{2x}}{2} - \\intxe^{2x}dx\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe use integration by parts once again to evaluate $\\displaystyle\\int xe^{2x}\\,\\textrm{d}x$. We take\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}u = x & ⟹\\frac{du}{dx} = 1 \\\\ \\frac{dv}{dx} = e^{2x} & ⟹v = \\int\\frac{dv}{dx}dx = \\inte^{2x}dx = \\frac{e^{2x}}{2}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the formula for integration by parts gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\intxe^{2x}dx &= \\intu\\frac{dv}{dx}dx \\\\\n&= uv - \\intv\\frac{du}{dx}dx \\\\\n&= x(\\frac{e^{2x}}{2}) - \\int(\\frac{e^{2x}}{2})(1)dx \\\\\n&= \\frac{xe^{2x}}{2} - \\frac{1}{2}\\inte^{2x}dx \\\\\n&= \\frac{xe^{2x}}{2} - \\frac{e^{2x}}{4} + D\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is an integral constant.\n\nSo we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\intx^{2}e^{2x}dx &= \\frac{x^{2}e^{2x}}{2} - (\\frac{xe^{2x}}{2} - \\frac{e^{2x}}{4} + D) \\\\\n&= \\frac{x^{2}e^{2x}}{2} - \\frac{xe^{2x}}{2} + \\frac{e^{2x}}{4} + C \\\\\n&= \\frac{e^{2x}}{4}(2x^{2} - 2x + 1) + C\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C =-D$."] [17592186068495 :question/problem "Evaluate the integral $\\displaystyle \\int x^2\\cos(3x) \\textrm{d}x$."] [17592186068495 :question/worked-solution "In this case, we define\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}u = x^{2} & ⟹\\frac{du}{dx} = 2x, \\\\ \\frac{dv}{dx} = \\cos (3x) & ⟹v = \\int\\cos (3x)dx = \\frac{1}{3}\\sin (3x)\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\intx^{2}\\cos (3x)dx &= \\intu\\frac{dv}{dx}dx \\\\\n&= uv - \\intv\\frac{du}{dx}dx \\\\\n&= (x^{2})(\\frac{1}{3}\\sin (3x)) - \\int(\\frac{1}{3}\\sin (3x))2xdx \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{3}x^{2}\\sin (3x) - \\frac{2}{3}\\intx\\sin (3x)dx\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAgain, we use integration by parts to evaluate $\\displaystyle \\int x\\sin(3x) \\textrm{d}x$. We take\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}u = x & ⟹\\frac{du}{dx} = 1, \\\\ \\frac{dv}{dx} = \\sin (3x) & ⟹v = \\int\\sin (3x)dx =-\\frac{1}{3}\\cos (3x)\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the formula for integration by parts gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\intx\\sin (3x)dx &= \\intu\\frac{dv}{dx}dx \\\\\n&= uv - \\intv\\frac{du}{dx}dx \\\\\n&= x(-\\frac{1}{3}\\cos (3x)) - \\int(-\\frac{1}{3}\\cos (3x)) \\cdot 1dx \\\\\n&=-\\frac{1}{3}x\\cos (3x) + \\frac{1}{3}\\int\\cos (3x)dx \\\\\n&=-\\frac{1}{3}x\\cos (3x) + \\frac{1}{3}(\\frac{1}{3}\\sin (3x)) + C_{1} \\\\\n&=-\\frac{1}{3}x\\cos (3x) + \\frac{1}{9}\\sin (3x) + C_{1}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C_1$ is a constant of integration.\nSo we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\intx^{2}\\cos (3x)dx &= \\frac{1}{3}x^{2}\\sin (3x) - \\frac{2}{3}\\intx\\sin (3x)dx \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{3}x^{2}\\sin (3x) - \\frac{2}{3}(-\\frac{1}{3}x\\cos (3x) + \\frac{1}{9}\\sin (3x) + C_{1}) \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{3}x^{2}\\sin (3x) + \\frac{2}{9}x\\cos (3x) - \\frac{2}{27}\\sin (3x) - \\frac{2C_{1}}{3} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{27}((9x^{2} - 2)\\sin (3x) + 6x\\cos (3x)) + C\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nC = -\\dfrac{2C_1}{3}\n$$"] [17592186068496 :question/problem "Evaluate the integral $\\displaystyle \\int_1^e 32x^3(\\ln x)^2 \\textrm{d}x$."] [17592186068496 :question/worked-solution "We'll work out the indefinite integral first, and then proceed to work out the definite integral.\n\nIn this case, we define\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}u = (\\ln x)^{2} & ⟹\\frac{du}{dx} = \\frac{2\\ln x}{x}, \\\\ \\frac{dv}{dx} = 32x^{3} & ⟹v = \\int32x^{3}dx = 8x^{4}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int32x^{3}(\\ln x)^{2}dx &= \\intu\\frac{dv}{dx}dx \\\\\n&= uv - \\intv\\frac{du}{dx}dx \\\\\n&= (\\ln x)^{2}(8x^{4}) - \\int(8x^{4})(\\frac{2\\ln x}{x})dx \\\\\n&= 8x^{4}(\\ln x)^{2} - 16\\intx^{3}\\ln (x)dx\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe use integration by parts once again to evaluate $\\displaystyle\\int {x^3\\ln(x)} \\textrm{d}x$. We take\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}u = \\ln (x) & ⟹\\frac{du}{dx} = \\frac{1}{x}, \\\\ \\frac{dv}{dx} = x^{3} & ⟹v = \\intx^{3}dx = \\frac{x^{4}}{4}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the formula for integration by parts gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\intx^{3}\\ln (x)dx &= \\intu\\frac{dv}{dx}dx \\\\\n&= uv - \\intv\\frac{du}{dx}dx \\\\\n&= \\ln (x)(\\frac{x^{4}}{4}) - \\int(\\frac{x^{4}}{4})(\\frac{1}{x})dx \\\\\n&= (x^{4}\\ln (x))/(4) - \\frac{1}{4}\\intx^{3}dx \\\\\n&= (x^{4}\\ln (x))/(4) - \\frac{x^{4}}{16} + C_{1}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C_1$ is an integral constant. So, we get that the indefinite integral is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int32x^{3}(\\ln x)^{2}dx &= 8x^{4}(\\ln x)^{2} - 16\\intx^{3}\\ln (x)dx \\\\\n&= 8x^{4}(\\ln x)^{2} - 16((x^{4}\\ln (x))/(4) - \\frac{x^{4}}{16} + C_{1}) \\\\\n&= 8x^{4}(\\ln x)^{2} - 4x^{4}\\ln (x) + x^{4} - 16C_{1} \\\\\n&= x^{4}(8(\\ln x)^{2} - 4\\ln (x) + 1) + C\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C = -4C_1$. Finally then, we can work out the definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int_{1}^{e}32x^{3}\\ln (x)dx &= \\left.x^{4}(8(\\ln x)^{2} - 4\\ln (x) + 1)\\right|_{1}^{e} \\\\\n&= [(e)^{4}(8(\\ln (e))^{2} - 4\\ln (e) + 1)] - [(1)^{4}(8(\\ln (1))^{2} - 4\\ln (1) + 1)] \\\\\n&= [e^{4}(8 - 4 + 1)] - 1 \\\\\n&= 5e^{4} - 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [] "immutable_fields" [] "no_history" []}
